H7223:
1458) (RSh) ac: Inherit co: Head ab: ?: The pictograph is a picture of the head. The head of the tribe (chief) or family (father) is passed from generation to generation. The head grants permission for the betrothal of his daughters and determines the inheritor of the tribe or family. The head of a person, place, thing or time. (eng: raise - with the exchange of the s and sh)
ef1) (RY-A-ShH) - Beginning: The head of a space such as the head of a river or time such as an event. [freq. 185] |kjv: first, former, beginning, chief, before, old, foremost, aforetime| {H7223}
ejm) (RY-A-ShWN) - First: The head of a time or position. [freq. 185] |kjv: first, former, beginning, chief, before, old, foremost, aforetime| {H7223}
